.TH "FLOX\-GENERATIONS\-HISTORY" "1" "" "" "Flox User Manuals"
.SH NAME
flox\-generations\-history \- Show the change log for the current
environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
flox [<general\-options>] generations history
     [\-d=<path> | \-r=<owner/name>]
     [\-u]
     [\-\-json]
     [\-\-no\-pager]
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the change log for the current environment.
.PP
For environments pushed to FloxHub, every modification to the
environment creates a new generation of the environment.
It\(cqs also possible to change the current generation by using
\f[CR]flox generations switch\f[R] or
\f[CR]flox generations rollback\f[R].
.PP
\f[CR]flox generations history\f[R] prints what generation has been the
current generation over time.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-json\f[R]
Render generations as JSON.
\f[B]Attention:\f[R] the output is not guaranteed to be stable.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-no\-pager\f[R]
Explicitly disable paged output
.SS Environment Options
If no environment is specified for an environment command, the
environment in the current directory or the active environment that was
last activated is used.
.TP
\f[CR]\-d\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-dir\f[R]
Path containing a .flox/ directory.
.TP
\f[CR]\-r\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-reference\f[R]
A FloxHub environment, specified in the form \f[CR]<owner>/<name>\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]\-D\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-default\f[R]
Use your default environment (\f[CR]<your\-user>/default\f[R]).
When unauthenticated in an interactive context, you will be prompted to
log in.
In non\-interactive contexts (e.g., scripts or CI), this flag will fail
with an error when authentication is missing.
.TP
\f[CR]\-u\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-upstream\f[R]
Operate on the environment on FloxHub, rather than a local reference.
.SS General Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
Prints help information.
.PP
The following options can be passed when running any \f[CR]flox\f[R]
subcommand but must be specified \f[I]before\f[R] the subcommand.
.TP
\f[CR]\-v\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-verbose\f[R]
Increase logging verbosity.
Invoke multiple times for increasing detail.
.TP
\f[CR]\-q\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-quiet\f[R]
Silence logs except for errors.
